1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,100
Patriarchy is what drives people to commit a lot of the acts that lead us to prison.

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:07,660
And patriarchy is what leads us to believe in prisons in the first place.

3
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,040
I'm not even going to talk. Keep going.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,020
In my cultural context, as a young person who grew up in L.A.,

5
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:16,780
I was seeking to be a worthwhile human by being a quote unquote real man.

6
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:20,660
And real men had money and I was broke living in cars and shit.

7
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,500
So I decided to rob stores, you know, as a culture.

8
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:26,960
We also believe that domination is power.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:32,800
So when somebody, quote unquote, hurts us, and I put it in quotes because most people in L.A. were not affected by my robbery at all.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,860
We have to, quote unquote, hurt them back in order for there to be, quote unquote, justice.

11
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,900
And that is it is upon that idea that we build these castles of shame that we call prisons.

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:48,780
But if we saw power as connection, if we saw power as integrity, then rather than like I need to dominate you and force this, quote unquote, badness out of you,

13
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,680
it would be like you are a legitimate human being trying to suit your needs just like I am.

14
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:57,920
So what need are you trying to suit and what needs to be transformed so you can do that in a way that doesn't harm others?

